IMPORT prelude

-- Section 54 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): the standard scales for penalties and expiation fees.
-- The table has no header row: its left column holds an expression and its right column the meaning of that expression.
-- Each row is held as data, with the division, the kind and the amount read out of the printed words.
-- Imprisonment is held in months and a fine or fee in dollars.

§ `Section 54 -- Standard scales for penalties and expiation fees`

DECLARE `Kind of scale entry` IS ONE OF
    imprisonment
    fine
    `expiation fee`

DECLARE `Row of the table in section 54` HAS
    expression                  IS A STRING
    meaning                     IS A STRING
    division                    IS A NUMBER
    kind                        IS A `Kind of scale entry`
    `amount`                    IS A NUMBER
    `amount is a ceiling`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `line in the text file`     IS A NUMBER

-- src:582 | | Division 1 imprisonment | a term of imprisonment not exceeding 15 years |
@ref s 54 table row 1 (src:582)
`s 54 row 1` MEANS `Row of the table in section 54` WITH
    expression IS "Division 1 imprisonment"
    meaning IS "a term of imprisonment not exceeding 15 years"
    division IS 1
    kind IS imprisonment
    `amount` IS 180
    `amount is a ceiling` IS TRUE
    `line in the text file` IS 582

